# 4. Core Concepts

## 4.1 Scene

A scene is a persisted definition containing metadata, actions, execution rules and presentation information.

```swift
struct AuraScene: Identifiable, Sendable, Codable, Equatable {
    let id: AuraSceneID
    var name: String
    var icon: AuraSceneIcon
    var roomIDs: Set<AuraRoomID>
    var actions: [AuraSceneAction]
    var executionPolicy: AuraSceneExecutionPolicy
    var feedbackPolicy: AuraSceneFeedbackPolicy
    var isFavorite: Bool
    var createdAt: Date
    var updatedAt: Date
    var revision: Int
}
```

## 4.2 Action

An action is one requested change to one logical target or one scene-control operation.

Examples:

- Turn on Philips TV.
- Select HDMI 1.
- Wake Apple TV.
- Activate Hue scene Cinema.
- Set hallway lights to 15 percent.
- Execute a HomeKit scene.
- Wait 500 milliseconds.
- Verify TV power state.

## 4.3 Execution

An execution is one runtime instance of a scene.

```swift
struct AuraSceneExecution: Identifiable, Sendable {
    let id: AuraSceneExecutionID
    let sceneID: AuraSceneID
    let sceneRevision: Int
    let startedAt: Date
    let source: AuraExecutionSource
    var state: AuraSceneExecutionState
    var actionResults: [AuraSceneActionResult]
}
```

## 4.4 Plan

A plan is the validated runtime graph produced from a scene definition before commands are sent.

The plan resolves:

- Logical devices to active control routes.
- Capabilities to plugin commands.
- Dependencies between actions.
- Parallel groups.
- Timeouts.
- Retry policy.
- Preconditions.
- Unsupported actions.

