# 8. Action Groups

Scenes shall support explicit action groups.

```swift
struct AuraActionGroup: Identifiable, Sendable, Codable, Equatable {
    let id: AuraSceneActionID
    let mode: AuraActionGroupMode
    let actions: [AuraSceneAction]
    let failurePolicy: AuraActionFailurePolicy
}

enum AuraActionGroupMode: String, Sendable, Codable {
    case sequential
    case parallel
}
```

## 8.1 Sequential Group

Actions execute in order.

Use when:

- A later action depends on an earlier state.
- TV input selection requires the TV to be awake.
- Verification must happen after a command.

## 8.2 Parallel Group

Independent actions execute concurrently.

Use when:

- Turning on lights and waking Apple TV can happen independently.
- Multiple rooms can change at the same time.
- Parallel execution reduces perceived latency without introducing risk.

