# 10. Validation

Every scene must be validated before saving and again before execution.

Validation checks include:

- Scene has a non-empty name.
- Scene contains at least one action.
- Every target can be resolved or is intentionally optional.
- Target supports the requested capability.
- No recursive scene chain exists.
- No cyclic dependency exists.
- Timeouts are within allowed limits.
- Delays are within allowed limits.
- Parallel groups do not contain unsafe conflicts.
- Commands contain valid values.
- Required permissions are available.
- External scenes still exist.

```swift
struct AuraSceneValidationResult: Sendable {
    let isValid: Bool
    let errors: [AuraSceneValidationIssue]
    let warnings: [AuraSceneValidationIssue]
}
```

Warnings do not always block execution.

Examples:

- A device is currently offline.
- An action is optional.
- An external scene has not been refreshed recently.

