# 42. Acceptance Criteria

The Scene Engine is ready for initial release when:

- Users can create, edit, reorder and delete scenes.
- Scenes can contain actions from multiple integrations.
- Sequential and parallel groups execute correctly.
- Capability validation prevents unsupported commands.
- Duplicate taps do not create duplicate executions.
- Independent actions continue after unrelated failures under balanced policy.
- Required failures produce partial or failed results honestly.
- Scene execution progress is observable by the UI.
- Scene execution can be cancelled.
- Safe retries are bounded.
- Non-idempotent actions are never blindly retried.
- Timeouts are enforced without blocking the main actor.
- Execution history records sanitized summaries.
- Scene diagnostics include per-action results and selected routes.
- Automation Engine can execute scenes through the same API.
- Core flows pass on the target hardware.

